which actually feeds back in on itself. 

440
00:46:22,240 --> 00:46:26,320
It runs some function f and 
then writes back to itself. 

441
00:46:27,760 --> 00:46:42,400
For example, this might be an addition where 
you're adding a number every clock cycle. 

442
00:46:43,200 --> 00:46:49,920
This little circuit essentially sums all the 
numbers presented on different clock cycles. 

443
00:46:49,920 --> 00:46:54,320
The challenge is, if this plus 
takes too long, what can I do? 

444
00:46:54,320 --> 00:47:02,160
If I try to put a pipeline register 
right in the middle of it, it  

445
00:47:05,600 --> 00:47:08,800
