actually have two different running sums. 

447
00:47:12,880 --> 00:47:17,760
I'll end up with a running sum of the even 
numbers and a running sum of the odd numbers. 

448
00:47:18,640 --> 00:47:25,760
This constraint—where I have a loop in my logic, 
which all chips have somewhere—is the hardest  

449
00:47:25,760 --> 00:47:29,280
thing to address and sets the clock cycle.
I don't understand why it would be  

450
00:47:29,280 --> 00:47:30,960
a problem to have that.
I'm not even sure what it  

451
00:47:30,960 --> 00:47:36,000
would mean to have a register there.
Is it a sort of atomic operation? 

452
00:47:36,560 --> 00:47:41,040
Well, plus is not really atomic.
As you just demonstrated. 

453
00:47:41,040 --> 00:47:45,200
It took a whole lot of work to do a summation.
You can take the early parts of that work,  

454
00:47:45,840 --> 00:47:48,320
