460
00:48:24,160 --> 00:48:27,520
As a logic designer, the chip 
architect sets the clock cycle. 

461
00:48:28,240 --> 00:48:35,600
For example, the primitives you get from TSMC 
are on the order of AND gates or full adders. 

462
00:48:36,800 --> 00:48:46,720
It depends a lot on voltage and which library you 
choose, but generally you can have about 10, 20,  

463
00:48:46,720 --> 00:48:51,760
or 30 of these sequentially in a clock cycle.
These primitives are very fast,  

464
00:48:51,760 --> 00:48:57,840
